From: local
Subject: [PATCH] soc: rockchip: pm_domains: do not touch QoS on power transitions

On the RK3566 in the JP TV Box 3566 the power-down path of the npu domain
hangs the machine: rockchip_pmu_save_qos() reads five QoS registers with
plain regmap_read()s, the read never returns on the AXI bus, and the CPU
ends up spinning with interrupts disabled inside genpd_power_off_work_fn.
The kernel then dies right after "calling rtc_hctosys", where
clock_was_set() -> smp_call_function() waits forever for that CPU:

  rcu: INFO: rcu_preempt self-detected stall on CPU
  Workqueue: pm genpd_power_off_work_fn

A trace of the power-down steps (added temporarily with dev_info() prints,
dropped again once the culprit was known) showed rga and rkvenc completing
normally and the boot stopping right at "pm: 'npu' save_qos".

An MMIO access that stalls on the interconnect cannot be given a timeout,
so the only safe fix is not to access the QoS block around a power
transition at all.  The QoS values are a bus-priority tuning hint: not
saving/restoring them costs a little performance after a power cycle and
nothing else.

Also add rockchip,always-on so a board can pin a domain up (the pipe domain
is shared with the SATA combo PHY, and powering it down while a disk keeps
the PHY alive is not something this SoC handles gracefully).

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
@@ -319,9 +319,16 @@
 		if (!power_on) {
-			rockchip_pmu_save_qos(pd);
-			pd->qos_saved = true;
+			/*
+			 * Do not read the QoS block here.  On RK3566 that read
+			 * can stall on the AXI bus for the npu domain, and a
+			 * stalled MMIO access cannot be timed out - the CPU
+			 * then spins with interrupts disabled and the board
+			 * never finishes booting.  Skipping the save/restore
+			 * only loses a bus-priority tuning.
+			 */
+			pd->qos_saved = false;
 
 			/* if powering down, idle request to NIU first */
 			rockchip_pmu_set_idle_request(pd, true);
 		}
 
 		rockchip_do_pmu_set_power_domain(pd, power_on);
@@ -545,6 +552,14 @@
 	pd->genpd.flags = GENPD_FLAG_PM_CLK;
 	if (pd_info->active_wakeup)
 		pd->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP;
+	/*
+	 * Some domains must never be powered off.  The pipe domain is the
+	 * case in point: the SATA combo PHY is alive while a disk is
+	 * attached and the power-off sequence does not complete.  Boards
+	 * that need this set "rockchip,always-on" in the DT node.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(node, "rockchip,always-on"))
+		pd->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
 	pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
 
 	pmu->genpd_data.domains[id] = &pd->genpd;
